    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix `vllm run-batch` incorrectly reporting audio handler failures with status 400. Preserve the standard error mapping for transcription and translation requests, including 500 for engine failures and 503 for retryable errors.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Map audio handler exceptions through the existing batch error handling.\n- Preserve status 400 for audio download and request preparation failures.\n- Keep successful responses and handler-returned errors unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded a parameterized regression test covering transcription and translation with engine, retryable, and validation errors.\n\n- Before: all four 500/503 cases failed; both 400 cases passed.\n- After: **26 selected tests passed**.\n- All applicable pre-commit checks passed, including Ruff and mypy.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/launchers/test_run_batch.py \\\n  -k 'batch_audio or download_bytes or transcription_wrapper or upload_data' -q\n\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/entrypoints/launchers/run_batch.py \\\n  tests/entrypoints/launchers/test_run_batch.py\n```\n\n## Details\n\n`make_transcription_wrapper` previously caught both request preparation and handler exceptions, converting all failures to status 400.\n\nMove the handler call outside the preparation `try/except` so `run_request` applies the existing exception mapping. Audio download and request preparation errors retain their previous behavior.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>",
